// Detection: LSASS Credential Dumping via comsvcs.dll MiniDump
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1003.001 - OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory
// Data Source: Sysmon Event ID 1 - Process Creation
// Table: SysmonEvents
// Severity: High
//
// Logic:
// Detect rundll32.exe loading comsvcs.dll and calling its MiniDump export,
// a common living-off-the-land way to dump LSASS memory without extra tools.
// The export can also be called by ordinal (#24), so both forms are matched.
//
// Limitations:
// - Attackers can rename rundll32.exe or use other dump methods (procdump,
//   Task Manager, direct API calls), so this covers one technique only.
// - Pair with Sysmon Event ID 10 (ProcessAccess to lsass.exe) for better coverage.

SysmonEvents
| where EventID == 1
| where Image endswith @"\rundll32.exe" or CommandLine contains "rundll32"
| where CommandLine contains "comsvcs.dll"
| where CommandLine contains "MiniDump" or CommandLine contains "#24"
| project TimeCreated, Computer, User, Image, CommandLine, ParentImage, ProcessId
| sort by TimeCreated desc
